## Getting Started in 5 Minutes

### Prerequisites

- [.NET 10 SDK](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download)
- [Docker Desktop](https://www.docker.com/products/docker-desktop/) (for local dependencies)
- AWS CLI configured with a dev profile (or LocalStack — see below)

### 1. Set environment variables

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in the values:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env — at minimum set:
#   Forge__Authentication__ApiKey=your-local-dev-key
#   Forge__Secrets__UseSecretsManager=false
```

> All configuration keys and their env-var equivalents are documented in `.env.example`.

### 2. Start local dependencies

{{ if model.manifest.database != null }}
Start a local PostgreSQL instance (or use the provided compose file if one exists):

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name {{ model.manifest.product }}-postgres \
  -e POSTGRES_DB={{ model.names.namespace | string.downcase }} \
  -e POSTGRES_USER=dev \
  -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=dev \
  -p 5432:5432 \
  postgres:17
```

Apply migrations:

```bash
dotnet ef database update --project src/{{ model.names.namespace }}
```
{{ end }}

For Genesis modules (AWS), you can use [LocalStack](https://localstack.cloud) for local development:

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name localstack \
  -e SERVICES=secretsmanager,s3,stepfunctions \
  -p 4566:4566 \
  localstack/localstack:latest
```

Then set `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=http://localhost:4566` in your `.env`.

### 3. Build and run

```bash
dotnet restore
dotnet build
dotnet run --project src/{{ model.names.namespace }}
```

The service starts on:
- gRPC: `https://localhost:7001`
- Health check: `http://localhost:8080/healthz`

### 4. Verify the service is up

```bash
# Health check
curl http://localhost:8080/healthz

# gRPC reflection (lists available services)
grpcurl -plaintext localhost:8080 list
```

### 5. Run tests

```bash
dotnet test tests/{{ model.names.namespace }}.Tests \
  /p:CollectCoverage=true \
  /p:CoverletOutputFormat=cobertura \
  /p:Threshold=90
```

---

## Authentication

The service uses API key authentication. Pass the key in the `X-Api-Key` header:

```bash
grpcurl \
  -H "X-Api-Key: your-local-dev-key" \
  -d '{}' \
  localhost:7001 {{ model.manifest.service_name | string.replace "-" "_" }}.{{ model.names.dot_net_class_name }}Service/Hello
```

